WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.920
Speaker 1: Florida Governor Ron DeSantis still
has not even announced that he is joining

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:10.480
the Republican presidential primary and his
candidacy continues to collapse.

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.800
Will hold on if it hasn't started.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:14.820
How is it collapsing?

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:17.290
The answer is recent polling.

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:19.100
You have to see this.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:23.119
It's actually I don't know that we've ever
seen anything like this.

00:00:23.119 --> 00:00:29.289
The green line on your screen pointing down
is Ron DeSantis is polling.

00:00:29.289 --> 00:00:33.570
And I'll give you the numbers if you're just
listening today, the purple line near the

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:39.110
top is Donald Trump, which continues to climb.

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:46.920
Something happened right around March 28th,
29/30, that has sent Donald Trump's Republican

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:51.460
polling up and Ron Desantis's Republican polling
down.

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:56.010
And this just so happens to have been the
moment where we learned Donald Trump would

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:57.870
be indicted and arrested.

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:04.890
Yes, I continue to believe that the arrest
and indictment of Trump does nothing for him

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:09.549
if he makes it to the general election in
November of 2024.

00:01:09.549 --> 00:01:15.820
But it is undeniably clear that it is doing
something for him in the Republican primary.

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:20.500
Ron DeSantis now down barely to 20% on average.

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:24.830
In recent polling, he had reached as high
as 30 to 33.

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:32.830
And Donald Trump continues to climb, now holding
55% of the Republican primary ballot.

00:01:32.830 --> 00:01:38.299
Understanding also that a bunch of the support
is among people who aren't even running at

00:01:38.299 --> 00:01:39.610
this point in time.

00:01:39.610 --> 00:01:43.750
Mike Pence has nearly 6%, but he's not running,
at least not right now.

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:47.640
Tim Scott has 2%, has not yet announced the
candidacy.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.869
Larry Elder has a one point.

00:01:49.869 --> 00:01:51.149
Chris Christie has one point.

00:01:51.149 --> 00:01:58.159
Christie may run, Hutchinson just shy of one
point and Sununu 7/10 of a point.

00:01:58.159 --> 00:01:59.360
So what does this mean?

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:06.649
Well, this means that unless Ron DeSantis
can take support from people currently supporting

00:02:06.649 --> 00:02:11.710
the failed former President Donald Trump,
he has no path to the nomination.

00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:18.480
Even if Ron DeSantis scoops up every bit of
the non-Trump vote, that only gets him to

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:24.850
45% of the Republican primary ballot, not
enough to win that nomination.

00:02:24.850 --> 00:02:32.319
So the question then becomes, how can de Santos
take voters that are already supporting Donald

00:02:32.319 --> 00:02:33.319
Trump?

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:37.550
And the answer may be he can't, that it's
really up to Trump to mess this thing up for

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:38.550
himself.

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:40.269
That's one perspective.

00:02:40.269 --> 00:02:46.230
The ways that it could get messed up for Trump,
for lack of a better term, could include more

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:51.560
arrests and indictments that definitively
take him off of the campaign trail.

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:52.750
Some kind of misstep.

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:57.769
But, I mean, listen, he's been found liable
of sexually assaulting and defaming a woman,

00:02:57.769 --> 00:03:00.970
and his support just keeps climbing among
Republican voters.

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:05.470
So I actually don't know what there is that
DeSantis could do.

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:08.000
What I can tell you won't help.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:13.360
DeSantis is the wishy washy approach that
he has taken where he'll sort of criticize

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:15.510
the failed former President Trump.

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:18.690
But he really stands for nothing and he won't
seriously do it.

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:19.740
This is just one example.

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:23.150
We looked at this earlier this week, and of
course, I apologize to those who have seen

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:24.150
this.

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:30.450
Here is DeSantis asked, Do you acknowledge
Trump really did lose in November of 2020?

00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:36.780
Do you acknowledge that the voter fraud that
Trump claims took place didn't actually take

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:41.069
place and DeSantis standing for nothing?

00:03:41.069 --> 00:03:42.069
Take a listen to this.

00:03:42.069 --> 00:03:43.069
You said there at.

00:03:43.069 --> 00:03:45.849
Speaker 2: Events in Iowa over the weekend
that the GOP is a culture of losing.

00:03:45.849 --> 00:03:52.190
Do you acknowledge the Trump loss in a lot
of this really tough stuff?

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:53.190
Right.

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:58.140
Well, I look at the last however many election
cycles, 2018, we lost the House.

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:00.260
True, we lost the Senate.

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:01.489
2020.

00:04:01.489 --> 00:04:03.260
Biden becomes president or go excuse me.

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:05.569
We lost the Senate in 2020.

00:04:05.569 --> 00:04:09.780
Biden becomes president and it's done a huge
amount of damage.

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:12.510
Very unpopular in 2022.

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:16.699
And we are supposed to have this big red wave
in Florida and Iowa.

00:04:16.699 --> 00:04:19.040
I didn't see a red wave across this country.

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:23.120
And so I think the party has developed a culture
of losing.

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:26.570
I think that there is not accountability.

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:28.970
And I think in Florida, we really showed what
it takes.

00:04:28.970 --> 00:04:29.970
Okay.

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:35.520
Speaker 1: I want to play the whole thing
and torture you all with Ron DeSantis.

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:41.680
This is not inspiring confidence that is not
going to bring over the Trump people who want

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:43.490
to hear him say.

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:49.170
Trump did win and this is not going to bring
over the non-Trump people who might want to

00:04:49.170 --> 00:04:51.800
hear him say, listen, we lost.

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:53.130
I wish we would have won.

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:56.190
But he lost and I'm running so that we can
actually win.

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:57.750
It's not going to convince anyone.

00:04:57.750 --> 00:04:59.330
Also, an unforeseen.

00:04:59.330 --> 00:05:05.650
Error for Ron DeSantis as he keeps going with
this anti-woke stuff, which might play okay

00:05:05.650 --> 00:05:07.960
among Florida Republicans.

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:14.491
But when you pull the country, the country
is not anti-woke in the way that Ron DeSantis

00:05:14.491 --> 00:05:15.910
is acting as they are.

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:20.949
Here is DeSantis yesterday talking about banning
gender study.

00:05:20.949 --> 00:05:21.949
What this.

00:05:21.949 --> 00:05:26.150
Speaker 2: Bill is saying is, you know, some
of these niche subjects like critical risk,

00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:27.150
the.

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:28.150
Speaker 1: Word is niche, sir.

00:05:28.150 --> 00:05:30.280
Speaker 2: Niche is theory.

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:36.259
Other types of deep niche EAI infused courses
and majors.

00:05:36.259 --> 00:05:37.550
Florida's getting out of that game.

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:44.900
If you want to do things like gender ideology,
go to Berkeley, go to some of these other

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:45.900
places.

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:47.900
That's fine.

00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:51.900
Speaker 1: It's fine.

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:52.900
Yeah.

00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:57.030
And by the way, I understand that both both
niche and niche are acceptable pronunciations

00:05:57.030 --> 00:06:00.810
in 2023 for that word that people have.

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:02.120
The country has been polled.

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:03.120
Okay?

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:12.259
And it's not at all evident that just because
Youngkin won in Virginia on this, you know,

00:06:12.259 --> 00:06:19.849
anti anti-woke campaign platform and because
DeSantis did well in Florida, it is not at

00:06:19.849 --> 00:06:24.720
all clear that that is going to win you a
presidential election or even a Republican

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:30.090
primary nationally, because for the most part,
the country, by roughly a 6040 margin is on

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:31.690
the woke side of things.

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:37.880
So to get back to our question, you look at
the numbers, you see the DeSantis collapse.

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:40.250
What can turn it around?

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:46.650
DeSantis may believe that simply announcing
a run is going to turn this around.

00:06:46.650 --> 00:06:52.690
He may be right that announcing that he is
running might push him from 20 to 25 in the

00:06:52.690 --> 00:06:54.220
Republican primary.

00:06:54.220 --> 00:07:00.120
It might push him from 20 to 28, maybe even
to 30 in the Republican primary.

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:01.880
But you don't win with that.

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:07.910
And it is not at all clear that he has a path
to denying Trump the roughly 50 plus percent

00:07:07.910 --> 00:07:08.910
that he needs.

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:13.770
So things not going well for Ron DeSantis,
things going very well for Donald Trump in

00:07:13.770 --> 00:07:15.250
the Republican primary.

00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:20.000
Rumor has it DeSantis, if he is going to announce
maybe doing so in the next 7 to 10 days, we

00:07:20.000 --> 00:08:05.700
will watch it.

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:22.430
I will, of course, let you know.

